Mojo::Rennari
=============

Real-time WebSocket messaging for Mojolicious applications, named after
the Old Norse rennari — "runner, messenger, envoy".

A small, secure, MessagePack- or JSON-framed event layer. Not a Socket.IO
clone, not a drop-in replacement. It offers the features that matter for
a Mojolicious app: custom events, rooms, namespaces, acknowledgements,
reconnection, and connection state recovery.

Ships both a server and a client.

STATUS

Working. Server and client are tested against each other. The protocol
is implemented in seven languages; this repo is the reference
implementation and the origin of the specification.

    Protocol specification: PROTOCOL.md

Other implementations:

    rennari-client-js   JavaScript client
    rennari-server-js   JavaScript server
    rennari-go          Go client and server
    rennari-py          Python client and server
    rennari-rs          Rust client and server
    rennari-java        Java client and server

INSTALL

    cpanm Mojo::Rennari

Or with carton:

    carton install

QUICK START — SERVER

    use Mojolicious::Lite;
    use Mojo::Rennari::Server;

    my $rennari = Mojo::Rennari::Server->new(
        auth_cb => sub {
            my $c = shift;
            my $token = $c->param('token') // return undef;
            return undef unless $token eq 'secret';
            return { id => 'user-1' };
        },
    );

    $rennari->on('chat' => sub {
        my ($c, $payload) = @_;
        $c->rennari->join($payload->{room});
        $c->rennari->broadcast_to_room($payload->{room}, 'chat', $payload);
    });

    websocket '/ws' => sub {
        my $c = shift;
        $rennari->websocket_route($c);
    };

    app->start;

QUICK START — CLIENT

    use Mojo::Rennari::Client;
    use Mojo::IOLoop;

    my $client = Mojo::Rennari::Client->new(
        url => 'ws://127.0.0.1:3000/ws?token=secret',
    );

    $client->on('connect' => sub {
        my $c = shift;
        $c->of('/chat')->send('hello' => { n => 1 });
    });

    $client->on('reply' => sub {
        my ($c, $payload) = @_;
        say 'reply: ', $payload->{ok};
    });

    my $chat = $client->of('/chat');
    $chat->on('hello_back' => sub {
        my ($c, $payload) = @_;
        say 'chat: ', $payload->{got}{n};
    });

    $client->connect;
    Mojo::IOLoop->start;

CORE CONCEPTS

Frames

Every message is a map:

    { e => $event, d => $payload, id => $id?, o => $offset?, n => $namespace? }

- e — event name, [A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{1,64}
- d — payload, any MessagePack- or JSON-encodable value
- id — optional acknowledgement id
- o — optional offset, present when recovery is enabled
- n — optional namespace, omitted for /

Serialized as MessagePack by default, or JSON if configured. Binary
WebSocket frames, always.

Authentication

auth_cb runs during the HTTP request, before the WebSocket upgrade. A
falsy return renders 401 and no socket is opened. The returned identity
is available to handlers via $c->stash('rennari_identity').

Events

    $rennari->on('smile' => sub {
        my ($c, $payload) = @_;
        return { ok => 1 };
    });

If the handler returns a value, it is sent back as {e: 'reply', d: $value}.

Handlers can send with a custom event name to one client, everyone, or a
room:

    $c->rennari->send_to_self('smile_back', { ok => 1 });    # to sender
    $c->rennari->send_to($id, 'ping', { ... });              # to one id
    $c->rennari->broadcast('system', { text => 'restart' }); # to all

Rooms

    $c->rennari->join('lobby');
    $c->rennari->leave('lobby');
    $c->rennari->broadcast_to_room('lobby', 'chat', $payload);
    $c->rennari->members_of('lobby');   # arrayref of ids

Rooms are per-namespace. lobby in /chat is not lobby in /admin. They
auto-create on first join, disappear when the last member leaves. No
policy in the framework: the application decides when to join or leave
from its own handlers.

Namespaces

Multiple logical channels over one WebSocket connection, like Socket.IO.
Each namespace has its own handlers, rooms, and members.

    my $chat = $rennari->namespace('/chat');
    $chat->on('message' => sub {
        my ($c, $payload) = @_;
        $c->rennari->broadcast_to_room('lobby', 'message', $payload);
    });

A client joins with {e: 'rennari_nsp', d: {name: '/chat'}}. The server
replies rennari_nsp_ok. Frames for a namespace the client has not joined
close the connection with code 4005.

Every frame the server sends carries the namespace in n. Both sides
dispatch by that field, so no connection state is involved.

Acknowledgements

A client can send an id with any event. The server replies
{e: 'rennari_ack', d: {id: $id}} after the handler succeeds. If the
handler dies, no ack is sent, and the client's retry loop resends.
Duplicate delivery is possible; the framework does not deduplicate.
Handlers should be idempotent if retries are used.

Lifecycle hooks

    $rennari->on_connect(sub { my ($c, $identity) = @_; });
    $rennari->on_disconnect(sub { my ($c, $identity) = @_; });
    $rennari->on_error(sub {
        my ($c, $kind, $detail) = @_;
        # $kind is 'bad_frame', 'unknown_event', or 'handler_error'
    });

Hooks that die are caught and logged; they cannot break the connection.

Recovery

    my $rennari = Mojo::Rennari::Server->new(
        recovery        => 1,
        recovery_window => 120,
    );

Off by default. When enabled, the server issues a private session id at
handshake and tracks an offset on every outbound frame. If a connection
drops, its session is kept for recovery_window seconds with any frames
that would have been sent to it buffered. On reconnect, the client sends
{e: 'rennari_resume', d: {session_id, offset}}. The server replays missed
frames, re-attaches namespaces and rooms, and replies rennari_resumed.
A session that is unknown, expired, or still attached to a live connection
gets rennari_resume_failed.

Without recovery, no o field is present on any frame and no session
frame is sent.

Mock mode

    my $rennari = Mojo::Rennari::Server->new(mock => 1);

Skips auth_cb, synthesizes an identity, and ignores unknown events.
Refused automatically when MOJO_MODE is production, unless
force_mock => 1. For development only.

CLIENT

    my $client = Mojo::Rennari::Client->new(
        url         => 'ws://example.com/ws',
        serializer  => undef,           # msgpack or 'json'
        ack_timeout => 5,
        retries     => 3,
    );

    $client->on('connect' => sub { my $c = shift; ... });
    $client->on('disconnect' => sub { my ($c, $info) = @_; ... });
    $client->on('error' => sub { my ($c, $msg) = @_; ... });
    $client->on('ack_timeout' => sub { my ($c, $info) = @_; ... });
    $client->on('recovered' => sub { my ($c, $info) = @_; ... });

    $client->on('event', sub { my ($c, $payload) = @_; ... });
    $client->send('event', { ... });

    my $nsp = $client->of('/chat');
    $nsp->on('message', sub { my ($c, $payload) = @_; ... });
    $nsp->send('message', { ... });

    $client->emit_with_ack('ping', { ... }, sub {
        my ($result, $err) = @_;
    });

    $client->connect;
    $client->disconnect;
    $client->is_connected;
    $client->session_id;     # set after connect when recovery is on
    $client->last_offset;    # highest offset seen

The client declares all non-default namespaces it has registered
immediately after connecting.

CLOSE CODES

- 4002 — bad frame (decoder rejected the bytes)
- 4003 — unknown event (no handler registered, non-mock)
- 4004 — handler died
- 4005 — unknown namespace, or frame for a namespace the client has not joined
- 4006 — recovery disabled but client sent rennari_resume

CONFIGURATION

Server:

    my $rennari = Mojo::Rennari::Server->new(
        auth_cb            => sub { ... },   # required in production
        serializer         => 'msgpack',     # or 'json'
        max_bytes          => 64 * 1024,     # max frame size
        recovery           => 0,             # enable session recovery
        recovery_window    => 120,           # seconds
        inactivity_timeout => 300,           # seconds, overrides Mojo's 30s default
        mock               => 0,             # development only
        force_mock         => 0,             # overrides production refusal
        logger             => Mojo::Log->new,
    );

Client:

    my $client = Mojo::Rennari::Client->new(
        url          => 'ws://...',
        serializer   => undef,       # msgpack or 'json'
        max_bytes    => 64 * 1024,
        ack_timeout  => 5,
        retries      => 3,
        mock         => 0,
        force_mock   => 0,
        logger       => undef,
        ua           => undef,       # Mojo::UserAgent
    );

SECURITY

- Auth runs before the upgrade. Failed auth = 401, no socket opened.
- Frames are validated on decode: event name grammar, id format, offset
  format, namespace grammar, size limit. Any violation closes the
  connection with a specific code.
- Decoder never dies on untrusted input.
- MessagePack max_bytes cap is checked before unpack.
- The serializer is chosen per server, not per connection. A mismatch
  fails decode like any other malformed frame.
- mock is refused in production.

The framework does not implement rate limiting. If you expose the server
publicly, add per-connection frame budgets at the application level, or
use a reverse proxy.

EXAMPLES

examples/app.pl and examples/client.pl are a runnable server and client
pair. examples/app_production.pl and examples/client_production.pl show
first-message authentication instead of URL query parameters.

    carton exec -- perl -Ilib examples/app.pl daemon -l http://127.0.0.1:3000
    carton exec -- perl -Ilib examples/client.pl 3000

